here in Germany dozens of protests  against coronavirus restrictions took  place in several cities on Monday night  there were a large number of arrests in  the city of effort several police  officers were injured when they were  attacked with bottles and fireworks  the protests which for the most part are  illegal have become more militant in  recent weeks restrictions on public life  have been increased for those who are  not vaccinated Plans by Germany's new  government to introduce mandatory  vaccinations for certain workers have  further incensed the protesters  [Music]  so for more on this we're joined by  political correspondent Hans brunt from  our parliamentary Studio here in Berlin  Hans how significant are these protests  and do we know who the organizers are  well we have to say that it is a very  small minority in German society that  attends these protests and also a small  minority of people that are in fact  against vaccinations against these  restrictions but still they are very  loud they are very  noticeable and they do take place all  across the country they were really  dozens of protests last night ranging  from a couple of hundred people to a  couple of thousands in several cities  especially in Eastern Germany and they  have become more militant there have  been recent protests with torches that  were lit in front of the residences of  for instance the health minister in the  Eastern State of Saxony so some of the  politicians involved have been attacked  almost personally so the the anger  amongst these protesters seems to be  increasing in their preparedness to  become more militant to engage in  violence so given that what has the  government's reaction been to these  protests  well there has been an increase in  police controls in the past these  protests have been not prohibited but  the the attempt has been to allow them  to take place without any significant  incidents nowadays in various regions  there is an attempt actually to stop  them and to arrest more people  especially in the light of the fact that  right-wing extreme right-wing groups are  concretingly participating in this  encoding for violence there's also some  concern in government about the telegram  messenger Dean Messenger Service this is  a service that is used that has open  groups that are used for organizing  these protests mainly by the far right  wing or the right-wing populist  alternative for Germany party and  there's an attempt to try and control  these groups but the messenger messenger  service is based in in the Arab in the  United Arab Emirates and it's very  difficult actually to get hold of them  hence and thank you so much for that  update
 

